.TH COREGLOWD 1 "2026-11-01" "coreglow 0.10.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
coreglowd \- lighting and fan service for the Corsair iCUE Commander Core XT and Commander CORE
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B coreglowd
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B coreglowd
runs as a systemd user service
.RB ( coreglowd.service )
and drives a Corsair iCUE Commander Core XT (or, experimentally, a Commander CORE)
over hidraw: it streams the
lighting of the profile in use (about 30 frames per second for moving
effects), sets the duty of fans 1 and 2 from their curves, and evaluates the
automatic switching rules. With motherboard sync on, it also sends the
lighting to an OpenRGB server. With night dimming on
.RB ( [night] ),
it lowers the brightness of everything between the two times.
.PP
On the Core XT the pump (fan port 6) stays at full speed while it runs; the
controller does that whenever the lighting is driven from the PC. On a
Commander CORE the pump has its own port and runs at the profile's
.B pump
speed (50\(en100 %), and the fans on ports 3\(en6 follow the profile's shared fan
setting. When the service stops, it stores the backup curve in the controller
(Core XT: fans 1 and 2 follow case probe 1; CORE: fans 1\(en6 follow the liquid
temperature; pump at 100 %) and returns it to hardware mode.
.PP
It listens on the control socket
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/coreglowd.sock
(only the user can open it), one text line per request:
.B set
.IR NAME ,
.BR test-fans ,
.B status
(the latest status as JSON) and
.B watch
(a JSON status line every time one is published).
.BR coreglow ,
.B coreglowctl
and the tray use it, and fall back to the files when it isn't there.
.PP
It notices changes to its files on every frame, and reconnects by itself when
the controller disappears (unplugged, or passed to a virtual machine).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/coreglow/config.toml
Profiles and settings; created from
.I /usr/share/coreglow/config.toml
on first start.
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/coreglow-status.json
Live values, written every second.
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/coreglow-test-fans
Touching this file runs the fans at full speed for 5 seconds.
.SH NOTES
Needs read and write access to the controller's hidraw node; the package's
udev rule grants it to the user at the seat. Don't run
.B liquidctl status
or OpenRGB's Corsair detection while it runs: they switch the controller's mode.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR coreglowctl (1),
.BR coreglow (1)
